    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Les questions avec be",
     "md": "On **inverse** le sujet et be.\n\n- She **is** ten. → **Is** she ten? — Yes, she is.\n- They **are** in class. → **Are** they in class? — No, they aren't."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 1 : question avec be",
     "statement": "Pose la question : « Amina is in Bamenda. »",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "On met **is** au début : Is Amina…"
      },
      {
       "md": "Question complète : **Is Amina in Bamenda?**"
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**Is Amina in Bamenda?**"
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Les questions au présent simple",
     "md": "On utilise **Do** (I, you, we, they) ou **Does** (he, she, it) + sujet + verbe de **base**.\n\n- **Do** you like rice? — Yes, I **do**. / No, I **don't**.\n- **Does** she live in Douala? — Yes, she **does**. / No, she **doesn't**.\n- **Where do** you live? — I live in Kribi."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 2 : poser la question",
     "statement": "Pose la question : « Paul plays football on Saturday. »",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "Paul = he : on utilise **Does**."
      },
      {
       "md": "Le verbe revient à la forme de base : **play**."
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**Does Paul play football on Saturday?**"
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Erreurs fréquentes",
     "md": "- « Does she likes tea? » est faux : après does, **pas de -s** : Does she like tea?\n- « Where you live? » est faux : il faut **do** : Where do you live?\n- Répondre « Yes, she likes » : la réponse courte est **Yes, she does**."
    },
